WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.120
- Thanks to CuriosityStream
for keeping Legal Eagle

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.310
in the air, get 40% off of
CuriosityStream and Nebula

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.820
with the link in the description.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.210
At the moment, there
is no cure or treatment

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.700
for COVID-19, but that hasn't stopped

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.910
some of the world's prominent experts

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:15.750
from claiming to have found a cure.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:16.890
Rodney Howard-Browne said.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.250
- If they sneeze it, it shoots it down

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.420
at like 100 miles an hour,

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.390
it'll neutralize it in a split second.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.530
- President Trump said.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.810
- A lot of people think
that goes away in April

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.230
with the heat, as the heat comes in.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.450
Typically that will go away in April.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:32.770
- Commissioner Culpepper said.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:34.620
- This sounds really
goofy, and it do to me too,

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.750
but it works, so you hold a
blow dryer in front of your face

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.060
and you inhale with your nose,

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.000
and it kills all the viruses in your nose.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.650
- And Kenneth Copeland said.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:47.736
- I execute judgment on you, COVID-19.

00:00:47.736 --> 00:00:49.980
I call you done!

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.790
- And President Trump also said.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:54.140
- And then I see the disinfectant,

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:56.590
and is there a way we can
do something like that?

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.500
By injection inside or,
or almost a cleaning?

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:03.913
- Et cetera.

00:01:03.913 --> 00:01:05.440
Now some of these clips are funny,

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.070
but they're also infuriating.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:09.810
People who promote snake
oil cures to COVID-19

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.900
prey on the sick and the vulnerable.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.590
A suggestion may seem harmless,

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.550
but encouraging people to
buy or take concoctions

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.680
that don't actually work
can cause lasting damage.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.310
You may be wondering
whether these people have

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:25.930
legal liability for promoting
these fake coronavirus cures.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:28.870
You've probably seen them on
Facebook from well-intentioned

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:31.530
aunts and debated them
in the comments section

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.780
of your local news station,
but let's talk about

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.500
what consequences these
people actually face.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.970
And oh yes, we are definitely
going to talk about

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.880
the president's question
about injecting bleach

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.945
and taking sunlight internally.

00:01:43.945 --> 00:01:46.695
(dramatic music)

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.170
Hey Legal Eagles, it's time
to think like a lawyer,

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:53.120
because there's a lot of
bad information out there,

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.860
and you may be thinking that
when people lie intentionally,

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:00.590
they face stiff legal consequences,

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.210
but it's important to note
that in the status quo,

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:08.270
the default position is that
you don't face liability for

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.710
free speech, that's what the
first amendment is all about,

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.170
and as we've covered many
times on this channel,

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:16.020
there generally is no
criminal or civil liability

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.410
for lying, generally speaking.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:19.920
The first amendment exists for a reason,

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.720
and I personally think
that that's a good thing.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.730
Generally, you're not going to be sued

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.740
for making false statements,
even potentially false

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.540
statements about cures and treatments,

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.430
even if you post them
to Facebook or YouTube

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:32.940
and your comments are viewed
by millions of people,

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.190
because that's what free speech is about.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:38.770
Free speech covers even
bad ideas and false ones,

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:40.560
and it's a problem because
the less people know

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.340
about these complicated subjects,

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.700
the more confident they are,

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.060
which is why today's video is
sponsored by Dunning-Kruger.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.480
- If you're like me, you
know more about managing

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.440
critically ill patients
than doctors and scientists

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.160
who dedicated their entire careers to it,

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:58.368
and so you should drink Dunning Kruger.

00:02:58.368 --> 00:03:02.610
It's the only choice for
the self-educated gentleman.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.677
Dunning Kruger, it'll give you confidence,

00:03:05.677 --> 00:03:08.910
although I don't think you
need any help with that.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:09.743
Cheers.

00:03:09.743 --> 00:03:12.600
- However there are times
when you go beyond that,

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.720
and especially when
you're selling products

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.300
and you're making specific claims about

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.130
what this product can and cannot do,

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.320
there are times when you might face civil

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.730
or sometimes even criminal liability.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:25.310
So let's talk about things
that are clearly criminal.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:28.900
Under 18 USC 1347, it is a crime to commit

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.090
healthcare fraud regarding providers,

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:33.590
and many people promote
cures and treatments

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:37.130
for COVID-19 online, so when
does this cross the line?

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:40.110
Well, the DOJ recently
filed its first legal action

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:43.100
for coronavirus-related
fraud under this statute

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.020
for a website that promised to give people

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:47.380
World Health Organization vaccine kits

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:50.580
in exchange for a
shipping charge of $4.95.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.130
Now I can be fairly certain
that these allegations

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:56.410
give rise to fraud if true,
because there isn't a vaccine

00:03:56.410 --> 00:04:00.930
for COVID-19, so when you try
and bilk medical providers

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.720
out of money for
something that isn't true,

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.060
that's healthcare fraud.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:06.180
And then there's the
old-fashioned kind of fraud,

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.550
where you knowingly lie to
people to get their money.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:11.160
There's the potential case
of the people who promote

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.760
garlic and honey as a
cure for coronavirus.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.280
Some even link to a journal article

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.620
that purports to provide evidence

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:19.110
for staking one's life on the garlic cure.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.990
Now the NIH journal article
that these people cite to

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.920
merely finds that garlic
extract had inhibitory effects

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:28.040
on bronchitis when tested
on chicken embryos,

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.480
which is not the same
as working on people,

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:33.330
and despite the pseudoscientific
basis for their claims,

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.310
these people generally
haven't committed fraud

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.050
because it's not illegal necessarily

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.860
to spread false information.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:42.020
But it is illegal to sell pills or cures

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:45.430
or products that are harmful
or have no real benefit

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.280
or aren't based on real things

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.810
when you make those kinds of claims.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.670
But I'm just a lawyer, what do I know?

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:53.090
Hey Dr. Francis, do honey and garlic

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:55.240
actually cure coronavirus?

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.300
- Honey and garlic have not been shown

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.980
to be effective in the
treatment of coronavirus.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.100
They have, however, been shown to be

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.820
more delicious than placebo

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.290
in seven out of 10 chicken marinades.

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:08.030
- Well even if these
people aren't put in jail,

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:10.580
hopefully they'll get their just desserts.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.770
Now that's fraud, but there
are other causes of action

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:15.340
that can attach, in certain
circumstances like these,

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.040
like negligent misrepresentation.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.980
In some cases, liability doesn't require

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:20.780
a knowing falsehood like fraud does.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:23.040
Negligent misrepresentation
differs from fraud

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.360
because it doesn't require a
showing of malicious intent

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:26.680
to recklessness by the defendant.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.280
Instead, it just requires
that the defendant's statement

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.440
be exaggerated or misstate certain facts,

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.490
and that these misstatements resulted from

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:36.100
the defendant's negligence
or lack of due diligence.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.210
But it also has to occur in a circumstance

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:41.130
that gives rise to a
duty between two parties.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.350
So again, simply going around the world

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:46.270
saying misstatements,
even based on negligence,

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:48.120
doesn't necessarily make you liable

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.640
for negligent misrepresentation

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:51.370
because you have to be in a relationship

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.610
with the people that are harmed

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.640
in relying on those statements.

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:57.490
Now I think our discussion of
negligent misrepresentation

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.260
should probably start
with the most powerful

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.860
person in the United
States, President Trump.

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:04.830
Because the president loves
to talk about chloroquine

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.560
and its derivative hydroxychloroquine

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:09.510
as a potential miracle cure for COVID-19.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.100
The drugs are already approved for use

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.270
to treat lupus and rheumatoid arthritis,

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:15.320
and preliminary research
has suggested that

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:18.590
the medications could be,
and I stress "could be" here,

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:20.850
helpful in treating COVID-19.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:23.210
Well the president and
Fox News have repeatedly

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:26.120
touted one small French
study of 20 patients

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:28.740
that followed the patients for six days.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.460
- It's currently being
prescribed in France,

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:32.650
where at least one study
suggests that it works.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.050
- Three of those 20 patients
ended up in the ICU,

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:36.220
one left the hospital,

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:39.150
one couldn't tolerate the
medication, and one died.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:41.640
But again, I defer to the experts here.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:46.000
Hey, Dr. Francis, is
hydroxychloroquine a miracle cure?

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.880
- The simple answer is we just don't know.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:49.780
It may be, it may not.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:52.870
It has shown some promise
in in vitro studies,

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:55.090
meaning in a laboratory, not in humans,

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.570
but at the time of recording,
there are no trials

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:00.170
convincingly showing
evidence of its efficacy.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:03.980
The French study that
got so much attention,

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:07.710
which was non-randomized,
has many, many problems,

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:10.330
chief being the
differential after follow-up

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:12.870
from the treatment time that
you were just hearing about.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.070
However, does that mean
that we need to just ignore

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.020
its findings entirely, of course not.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:20.090
Does it provide enough
evidence to start treating

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:22.020
everybody with hydroxychloroquine?

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:22.880
Definitely not.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:25.600
Does it provide enough
evidence to want to undertake

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:28.330
further research, absolutely,
and there are many trials

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:30.380
ongoing all over the world.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:33.080
The WHO is launching a huge multicenter,

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:36.690
multinational trial looking
at hydroxychloroquine,

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:40.560
and already in many hospitals
all over America and other

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.860
countries, hydroxychloroquine
is being given routinely.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:46.520
Now, that's partly because
we have few other options,

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.290
but it is being used, however,

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:51.820
all of that has to be in the
context of a clinical trial,

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.850
otherwise you just don't
know what you're doing,

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:55.560
you're not going to assess the response.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:59.670
Remember, 99% of people that
get this, or more, do not die.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:02.380
So to tease out the
effects of any treatment

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:03.910
is going to be complicated.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:06.820
We need answers to questions
like if it is effective,

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.540
in whom is it most effective?

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:10.950
In the sickest patients in intensive care

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:12.970
or is it better for prophylaxis?

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:15.860
We're potentially talking
about millions of people here,

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:17.870
so we need solid evidence.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.730
- Yeah, science is hard.

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.390
But the president said that he would

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.330
make the drug available
almost immediately,

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:25.261
and a day later, president Trump tweeted

00:08:25.261 --> 00:08:28.327
"hydroxychloroquine and
azithromycin, taken together,

00:08:28.327 --> 00:08:29.887
"have a real chance to
be one of the biggest

00:08:29.887 --> 00:08:32.137
"game changers in the history of medicine.

00:08:32.137 --> 00:08:34.890
"The FDA has moved mountains, thank you."

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:36.120
President Trump has
said the drugs are safe

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.270
and that patients have nothing
to lose by taking them.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:42.310
- The nice part is it's
been around for a long time,

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:47.310
so we know that if things
don't go as planned,

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:50.990
it's not going to kill anybody.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:53.600
- Hey Dr. Francis, do
people have nothing to lose

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:56.419
by taking a medication that's
been around for a while?

00:08:56.419 --> 00:08:58.870
- Hydroxychloroquine and
azithromycin have indeed

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:01.270
been around a long time, and so we do know

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.830
about their side effects,
and both of them can cause

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:05.980
a side effect called long QT,

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:08.100
which is where the electrics of your heart

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:11.000
can be affected, increasing
your risk of suffering

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:13.570
a potentially fatal cardiac arrest.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.160
Now we don't see this
complication very often

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.740
in patients taking
hydroxychloroquine for conditions

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:20.920
like lupus, which is
one of its common uses,

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.150
so that may lead you to
conclude that it's safe

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:24.990
in all settings, but remember,

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:26.850
these patients are being closely monitored

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:29.030
by their doctors, but more importantly,

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:32.490
they're a totally different
patient population to COVID-19.

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:34.800
COVID sufferers are much more unwell,

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.490
they have high rates of
cardiac and kidney involvement,

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:41.230
which could hugely increase their risk.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.430
- So what happens if people
rely on these statements

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:44.950
and then get sick or die?

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.230
Well unfortunately, we have the answer.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:50.100
An Arizona man died and
his wife was hospitalized

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:52.000
after they took chloroquine phosphate

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.300
in an attempt to avoid getting COVID-19.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:56.390
Although neither had any
symptoms of the virus,

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:58.520
they'd been listening to
president Trump and his allies

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:00.090
promote this, quote, cure.

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:01.460
- A tremendous breakthrough.

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:03.780
- The woman explained that she
knows she had some fish tank

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:06.330
cleaner and that one of the
ingredients was chloroquine.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.163
She said.

00:10:07.163 --> 00:10:09.950
- [Woman] I was in the
pantry stacking dog food,

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:13.137
and I just saw it sitting
in the back shelf and said

00:10:13.137 --> 00:10:16.730
"hey, isn't that that stuff
they're talking about on TV?"

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:19.060
Trump kept saying it
was, you know, basically,

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:20.760
it was pretty much a cure.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.310
- And her advice now?

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:25.681
- [Woman] Oh my god, don't take anything.

00:10:25.681 --> 00:10:30.340
Don't believe anything the
president says, and his people.

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:31.860
Call your doctor.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:33.780
- Now I've covered presidential immunity

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:36.710
in my prior video about
suing China or the president,

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:38.660
so this couple is not going be recovering

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.530
anything from the president any time soon,

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:41.820
but even if that weren't the case,

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:44.343
the president refrained from making any

00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:45.680
unqualifying factual
statements about the drug,

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:48.020
and of course, he wasn't
selling this drug,

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:49.960
and he wasn't in a position that gave rise

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.760
to a duty of care to the American people.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:55.750
Well, at least not a legal position

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.120
that gives rise to legal liability,

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.490
and recently there's
been a lot of literature

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:02.570
coming out that
hydroxychloroquine is likely

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:05.640
not a miracle cure, and that may lead to

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.610
many negative health consequences,

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:09.640
which is perhaps why
president Trump has turned

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:11.410
to other potential cures.

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:13.950
- Right, and then I see the disinfectant,

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:17.440
where it knocks it out
in a minute, one minute,

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:19.890
and is there a way we can
do something like that?

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:25.740
By injection inside or,
or, almost a cleaning,

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.580
because you see it gets in the lungs

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:29.700
and it does a tremendous number.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:31.160
So it's be interesting to check that,

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:33.880
so that you're gonna have
to use medical doctors,

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:36.560
but it sounds, it sounds
interesting to me.

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:39.610
- I have a lot of thoughts about this.

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:41.400
So many thoughts.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.730
Now I'll talk more about those thoughts

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:43.740
at the end of this video.

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:45.460
Now one of the defenses
that people have raised

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:47.010
about the president's remarks is that

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:49.760
he was only raising the
question about injecting bleach,

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:52.060
not actually suggesting
that people do that.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:53.770
Now believe it or not,
that actually parallels

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:56.370
a discussion in the legal
community about hearsay.

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:58.720
Recall that hearsay is
an out-of-court statement

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:01.180
used to prove the truth
of the matter asserted.

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:04.910
Key phrases there being statement
and the matter asserted.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.220
Then the question is a question.

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:08.320
Is a question a statement?

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:11.300
Is a question actually promoting
some sort of assertion?

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:14.360
I think most people probably
believe that a question

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:17.270
can in fact be a statement
for purposes of hearsay,

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:19.270
because there's often
a premise behind that.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:21.220
And with the president's remarks,

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:23.790
there is a premise behind that question,

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:26.360
the premise being that
people should, in fact,

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:28.030
consume bleach internally.

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:29.510
Don't do that.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:33.140
But as with the president's
remarks about hydroxychloroquine

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:35.100
liability probably wouldn't attach

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.550
to the president's remarks about ingesting

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:42.190
bleach or internally consuming
sunlight in some way.

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:44.670
And that result doesn't
change whether the person

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:47.530
talking about ingesting
bleach is a random person off

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:50.070
the street or if it's the
president of the United States,

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:52.590
even if there was, in
fact, apparently a spike

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:54.610
in people ingesting disinfectants

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:56.100
following the president's remarks.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:58.970
Now the obvious point here
is that no one should be

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:01.990
swallowing fish tank
cleaner or injecting bleach,

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:04.160
regardless of what the president says.

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.610
Thinking critically when
you're listening to cable news

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:09.700
or the president, regardless
of who is in the White House,

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.870
is probably always a good idea.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:13.810
But what else could, in fact,

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:16.440
give rise to criminal or civil penalties?

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.810
Federal mail and wire fraud
statutes are interpreted

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:21.510
broadly to prescribe, one,
causing the use of the mail

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:23.480
or wire communications, including email,

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:25.980
two, in conjunction with
a scheme to intentionally

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:28.200
defraud another of money or property.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.850
Three, by means of a material deception.

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:33.160
Wire and mail fraud are
crimes on their own,

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:35.730
but they also overlap with a
lot of other federal statutes.

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:38.620
People get confused that
often the same conduct

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:41.120
can give rise to a lot
of different crimes,

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:42.660
based on the various things,

00:13:42.660 --> 00:13:44.370
and it's the exact same conduct.

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:46.640
Essentially, if you use the
mail, telephone, or internet

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:49.230
to defraud people, you can
also be charged with mail

00:13:49.230 --> 00:13:51.570
and wire fraud, even though
it probably constitutes

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:53.520
regular fraud in a lot
of different contexts.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:55.580
In fact, the New York
Times just reported that

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:59.810
a doctor in southern
California was accused of fraud

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:02.236
for selling a cure to coronavirus

00:14:02.236 --> 00:14:07.000
which turned out to be
hydroxychloroquine and azithromycin.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:10.320
But the DOJ is pursuing a
lot of COVID-19 fraudsters

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.240
using these criminal
statutes, for example,

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.760
Keith Middlebrook, an actor
with an uncredited appearance

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:17.400
in Iron Man 2 and Thor,
was arrested by the FBI

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.090
for soliciting investments into a company

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:22.080
he said would market
phony COVID-19 medication.

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:25.620
Middlebrook promised investors
who spent a million dollars

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:30.240
returns of 200 to $300 million
as a conservative minimum.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:32.320
Middlebrook promoted
his scheme on Instagram,

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:35.360
where he had 2.4 million followers

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:37.000
and was charged with wire fraud.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.060
The lesson here, don't take medical advice

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:41.150
from non-medical professionals,

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.030
even if they were in a Marvel movie.

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:45.150
And also, sometimes don't trust even

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:47.490
the medical professionals
who promote a cure

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.127
that doesn't yet exist.

00:14:49.127 --> 00:14:51.820
But now is probably a
good time to talk about

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:54.240
the difference between false
advertising and puffery,

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:57.330
because a lot of people
say that they'll see an ad

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.890
and they'll think than
it's completely fraudulent,

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:03.060
but advertisers have a lot
of leeway, because again,

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:05.440
we generally don't want
to prosecute people

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:08.800
for just saying ideas or having opinions.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:10.850
And one of the big issues in this context

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:13.690
is objective, factual
statements which are false

00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:16.610
compared to subjective,
opinion-based statements.

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:18.180
People who are selling
products have a right

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:21.020
to talk them up, and even
embellish how great they are.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:23.340
However, the government has
the power to stop companies

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:26.040
from making claims that
are objectively false

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:27.940
or factual claims without basis.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:30.035
So let's choose an example at random.

00:15:30.035 --> 00:15:32.860
One of those random
late night infomercials

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:34.940
featuring, I don't know, My Pillow.

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:37.460
- Hello, I'm Mike Lindell,
inventor of My Pillow.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:39.450
- This is a classic example of both

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:42.410
potentially false advertising and puffery,

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:44.500
the sort of building up of a product

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:47.840
that doesn't constitute
actionable statements.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.970
Puffery consists of general description,

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:53.340
such as top quality, best,
or America's favorite.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:56.010
So Michael Lindell, creator of My Pillow,

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:58.950
and pal of president Trump,
has filled many infomercials

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.260
where he says his pillow will.

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:02.650
- [Michael] Ensure you get
the best sleep of your life.

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:05.490
- Now, this example has nothing
to do with the fact that

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:07.960
president Trump hosted this
guy in the Rose Garden,

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:10.260
but the statement is likely just puffery.

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:13.161
No one can truly prove
that a $40 My Pillow

00:16:13.161 --> 00:16:15.330
is gonna be better than
the pillow that you buy

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:17.030
at Big Lots for five dollars.

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:19.200
It's a largely subjective statement,

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:21.550
but our friend Mike Lindell
also ran into problems

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:23.380
with consumer protection
advocates when he made

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:25.900
specific health claims about My Pillow.

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:28.100
Lindell's many
advertisements asserted that

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:30.300
the pillow could help
people manage migraines,

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.600
anxiety, multiple sclerosis, PTSD,

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:34.950
restless leg syndrome,
acid reflux disease,

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:38.170
fibromyalgia, snoring, and
many other medical conditions.

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:42.293
Hey Dr. Francis, can a pillow
cure any of those ailments?

00:16:42.293 --> 00:16:45.360
- (sighs) No, it cannot
cure those ailments.

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:47.550
Look, just use a pillow
for the same reason

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:49.690
everybody else does, companionship.

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.680
- Yeah, so a consumer
protection group sued Lindell

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:54.990
for false advertising, and
although Lindell claimed

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.520
no wrongdoing, he settled
the case for almost a million

00:16:57.520 --> 00:16:59.750
dollars and removed the assertions that

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:02.100
My Pillow would help with
some of those diseases.

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:04.320
So what are the most
common ways to get sued

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:06.480
for false statements and bad products?

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.560
Well, the most common is
probably consumer fraud.

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:10.870
People who make false or
misleading product claims

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:12.770
face legal action from
both government authorities

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:15.400
and private consumers, and
although people on the internet

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:17.240
often say this is the
kind of thing that should

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:19.420
give rise to a class
action or we're gonna have

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:22.180
a class action to sue
China or president Trump,

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:25.170
this context in the consumer
protection environment

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:27.840
is the kind of thing that often gives rise

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:30.750
to class action lawsuits,
and several companies

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:32.700
are in hot water over outlandish claims

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:35.260
that they made that they
can cure coronavirus.

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:38.230
Take natural health
expert Sherrill Sellman.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:40.130
She appeared on televangelist Jim Bakker's

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:42.830
television show to sell
the Silver Solution,

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:45.740
a cure for COVID-19, supposedly.

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:48.260
- Well let's say it hasn't
been tested on this strain

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:52.150
of the coronavirus, but it's
been tested on other strains

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:55.890
of the coronavirus and has been able to

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:58.020
eliminate it within 12 hours.

00:17:58.020 --> 00:18:00.400
- And she made claims
that the Silver Solution

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:02.950
has been proven by the government
that it has the ability

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:05.430
to kill every pathogen it
has ever been tested on,

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:07.250
including SARS and HIV.

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:09.020
Jim Bakker then holds up the product

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:12.220
and suggests viewers pay
$80 to $125 to the show

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:14.140
in exchange for a bottle
of Silver Solution.

00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:17.690
The solution is a form of
colloidal silver, a liquid

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:20.740
supplement that contains
very tiny pieces of silver,

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:23.360
and not surprising, ingesting silver

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:24.960
can because be quite dangerous.

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:26.370
Here's a photo of someone who took

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:28.640
silver nose droplets for years.

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:33.640
Hey Dr. Francis, can silver
cure every disease known to man?

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:37.730
- No, it won't, but
even if it did, I mean,

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:40.000
sulfuric acid kills a lot of microbes.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.850
I wouldn't recommend taking that either.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:45.140
- Yeah, so this is potentially
a very clear-cut case

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:48.000
of consumer fraud, and
the DOJ in several states

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:51.120
have actually sent Bakker
cease and desist orders

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:52.900
for falsely promoting that Silver Solution

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:55.490
can cure, kill, or deactivate coronavirus

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.660
and boost elderly
consumers' immune systems,

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:00.900
when there is in fact no
vaccine, no pill, or potion

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:04.080
or other product that can
treat or cure coronavirus.

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:06.020
And similarly, state
and federal regulators

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:08.890
have also moved to stop
radio host and noted idiot

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:10.940
Alex Jones from selling fake cures,

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:14.040
including a toothpaste
that contains nano-silver.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:16.210
- The patented nano-silver we have,

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:18.210
the Pentagon has come out and documented,

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:20.577
and Homeland Security,
and said "this stuff kills

00:19:20.577 --> 00:19:23.400
"the whole SARS corona
family at point blank range."

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.550
Well of course it does,
it kills every virus.

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:28.270
- And after the inevitable
cease and desist letters,

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.880
Jones issued a disclaimer where

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:31.480
he walked back a lot of his claims.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.710
However, the videos of
these products are still up,

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:35.900
so Jones may not be out of hot water,

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:37.560
but this is a situation that

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:39.750
he finds himself in with some frequency.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:42.480
- Now is the time to get
ready and to get prepared

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:45.300
with emergency supplies
and items that are known

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:46.980
to boost your immune system.

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:49.130
- Now also there are causes of action

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.210
for things called unfair
business practices,

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:54.590
which overlap often with fraud
but are not exactly the same.

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:57.170
State and federal laws
allow a business to be sued

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:58.850
for unfair deceptive trade practices.

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:01.100
The phrase "unfair trade
practice" means any business

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:03.320
practice or act that is
deceptive, fraudulent,

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:05.390
or causes injury to a consumer.

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:07.780
So for example, a
Florida elected official,

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:11.160
of course Florida, Bryant
Culpepper claimed that you could

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:14.080
kill COVID-19 by aiming your
hair dryer up your nose.

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:16.090
- So you hold a blow dryer
in front of your face

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:18.500
and you inhale with your nose

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:20.719
and it kills all the viruses in your nose.

00:20:20.719 --> 00:20:21.552
(sighs)

00:20:21.552 --> 00:20:25.853
- Hey Dr. Francis, does a hair
dryer kill the coronavirus?

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:31.190
(sighs defeatedly)

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:33.760
Yeah, so incredibly dumb information,

00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:36.510
because of course, elected
official in Florida,

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:37.960
but can he be sued?

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:39.810
Well, probably not, like I said before,

00:20:39.810 --> 00:20:42.850
it's not illegal to say
something dumb or false,

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:44.840
and Culpepper is giving
out bad information,

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:47.810
but he's not selling a
product like a special

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:50.110
COVID-19-killing hair dryer.

00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:52.820
He's just a Floridian.

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:55.880
Never change, Florida man, never change.

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:58.200
But it can be hard to get
the word out on YouTube

00:20:58.200 --> 00:20:59.940
when we're dealing with
sensitive subjects,

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:02.290
because videos like these get demonetized,

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:04.430
but some people need to
be told not to inject

